 "script": "[curious] Do people visit your website... and then just leave?\n[seriously] Here's what's happening. A new visitor gives your website about three seconds. And in those three seconds... they're asking three questions. If they can't find the answers, they're gone.\nQuestion one. \"What do you do?\" So please... don't write \"Welcome to our website.\" Say it simply. \"We help restaurants in Texas with their bookkeeping.\"\nQuestion two. \"Is this for me?\" Say who you help, right at the top.\nQuestion three. \"What do I do next?\" Give them ONE clear button. Like \"Book a free call.\"\n[mischievously] Now try this. Open your homepage on your phone. Only look at the first screen. Can a stranger answer all three questions?\n[softly] If not... that's why people leave.\n[warmly] Comment \"FIX\", and I'll tell you the one thing I'd change on your homepage."
